WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
- No it's okay. It's okay, it's okay.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.090
It's okay, it's okay, it's okay.

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:04.083
Put more salt. Oh my god,
it's way too much salt.

00:00:04.083 --> 00:00:04.916
(shrieking)

00:00:04.916 --> 00:00:07.610
(rhythmic upbeat music)

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.770
In terms of cooking,

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.050
I don't really have any
professional experience.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.990
But I grew up cooking a lot at home

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.440
and people seem to like it.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.010
- The role I'm planning to play

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.890
is just very supportive friend.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.180
I'm gonna be an assistant,

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.670
I'm gonna be a cheerleader,

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:23.363
I'm gonna be a-sabotaging the competition.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:27.374
- We don't know exactly what
Adrienne's really good at,

00:00:27.374 --> 00:00:30.120
apart from the fact that she's
really good at everything

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.758
because she was the runner up of Top Chef

00:00:32.758 --> 00:00:35.870
and we're like the runner ups at nothing.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.680
- Competing against two people,

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.470
that's an extra set of
hands to get things,

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.490
an extra person to run around the kitchen

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:43.830
while the other one is cooking.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.256
So I was a little nervous about that.

00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:48.173
(electronic music)

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.790
- We're just hoping to
make something edible.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.653
Tell us, what's the challenge today?

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:58.150
Childhood favorite things
are usually easy to make,

00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.500
but then we looked at each other

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.360
and we were like, "One second."

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.620
- What do we eat as a child?

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:04.720
- Yes, very, very different things.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:05.553
- Good luck.

00:01:05.553 --> 00:01:07.070
I look forward to
competing against you two.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:08.693
- I look forward to taking you down.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.833
- Five minutes to grab things starts now.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.963
I see bacon.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.760
You can't see bacon and pass it up.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:16.880
There were a lot of options.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.910
There were a lot of things
that could have been done.

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:21.903
For childhood favorites,
I always need butter.

00:01:22.028 --> 00:01:24.380
I know when I was a kid, I loved cheese

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:26.443
so I'm gonna take some cheese.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:30.640
When I saw the sliced cheddar
and white American cheese,

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.320
I was like, "Yeah, I
think this will be fun."

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.673
I'm thinking heirloom tomato salad,

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.520
grilled cheese incorporated somehow,

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:39.190
and probably some kind of
tomato, red pepper vinaigrette.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:41.920
30 minutes is maybe not
enough time to do all that,

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.433
but let's give this a try.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.240
- We had very different childhoods.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.600
We don't eat the same kind of things.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:47.433
Ooh, ow.

00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:48.422
So there's cream.

00:01:48.422 --> 00:01:49.651
- Sriracha!

00:01:49.651 --> 00:01:51.080
- I never ate sriracha.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:51.913
- Oh really?

00:01:51.913 --> 00:01:53.050
Sriracha just makes
everything taste better

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:53.883
- No.

00:01:54.691 --> 00:01:55.524
(laughs)

00:01:55.524 --> 00:01:57.963
There's so much in there,
we can't decide on a dish.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.490
So we just start grabbing everything.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:00.323
- Just start grab everything.

00:02:00.323 --> 00:02:01.520
My strategy is grab everything

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.840
and then figure out what
we're gonna do later.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:04.420
Doesn't that make a lot of sense guys?

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:05.870
- Oh there's pasta!

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:08.350
- Macaroni and cheese is
something I loved growing up too.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:09.580
- Should we just make mac and cheese?

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.840
- We really should make mac and cheese,

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.290
but we gotta spice it up though.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.123
- Is there wine?

00:02:13.417 --> 00:02:14.250
(record scratches)

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.690
Oh, it was childhood favorites.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.733
- So we're thinking something fusion?

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.980
Mac and cheese and soy sauce?

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:22.380
And (laughing) I don't know.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:23.860
- We're gonna wing it.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.773
We're gonna make it good.

00:02:25.779 --> 00:02:26.960
(knife scraping)

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.060
- First thing I'm thinking,

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.890
before the countdown
begins to start cooking,

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:33.060
arrange my prep to take advantage

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:33.923
of the thirty minutes that we have.

00:02:33.923 --> 00:02:35.053
- Good to go?

00:02:35.293 --> 00:02:36.223
- We're good.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:37.443
- You sure?

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:39.496
- Yes!
- Top Chef is a reality show.

00:02:39.496 --> 00:02:41.180
How good are these chefs really?

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.930
I guess we're gonna find out today.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:45.560
We're ready to take you down.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:46.530
- Oh yeah. Bring it.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.030
Let's see about that (laughs).

00:02:50.134 --> 00:02:52.210
(intense rock music)

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:53.043
- Go grab salt.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.530
- Nnenna, can you pass
me the sun dried tomatoes

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.363
while you're there?

00:02:58.363 --> 00:02:59.300
It's right back on that shelf.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.400
All the way back.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.250
I promise.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:03.120
I actually needed
something from the pantry,

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.210
and she was right there,

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:05.680
so I thought, why not ask her?

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.140
Maybe she'll be nice
enough to pass it to me.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.033
But, no.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:10.500
Bam, sun dried tomatoes.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.333
Thanks, Nnenna.

00:03:11.333 --> 00:03:12.473
- You never help the enemy.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:13.989
- [Adrienne] Does not
play well with others.

00:03:13.989 --> 00:03:14.822
- Ever!

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.050
We've been waiting for the thingy to boil.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:17.883
The water.

00:03:17.883 --> 00:03:18.716
- [Nnenna] Right, okay.

00:03:18.716 --> 00:03:19.577
- You can just stand
there and look pretty.

00:03:19.577 --> 00:03:20.943
- Well that I can do.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.280
- You know how to grate cheese?

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:23.113
- Kind of.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.137
Yeah it is my first time
grating cheese actually.

00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:28.040
And I think I'm doing a pretty
great job at it right now.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:31.743
I did a professional level
grating cheese-er grater.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.416
I don't know.
- So what are you guys making?

00:03:33.416 --> 00:03:35.190
- We are going to make...

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.060
- Macaroni and cheese?

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:38.893
- Nice!

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.077
- It's the only one that we were like,

00:03:41.077 --> 00:03:42.610
"Okay we both had this as a child."

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:44.040
- What about you, you're making uh?

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:48.353
- I'm making grilled
cheese and tomato soup.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.433
A version of it.

00:03:49.573 --> 00:03:50.800
- (both) Ohhhh.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.053
- But like gourmet?

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.253
- No, you know. Just like kid-sy.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.290
- Well ours is gonna be gourmet, so.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.953
- [Adrienne] Oh, excuse me, playa.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:01.073
So right now, in this pot,

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:02.430
we're making our vinaigrette

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.830
which is gonna be our
version of the tomato soup.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:05.990
- What is a vinaigrette?

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:06.823
- I don't know.

00:04:06.823 --> 00:04:08.368
- So in the pot, we have some red onion,

00:04:08.368 --> 00:04:11.747
tomato, sun dried tomatoes, and oregano.

00:04:11.747 --> 00:04:15.533
Which is kind of like our tomato soup

00:04:15.533 --> 00:04:17.893
to go with our grilled cheese.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.500
- Wow, this is taking forever.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.100
You have to wait for the water to boil!

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.230
That's the most basic thing you need to do

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:24.368
before you cook pasta.

00:04:24.368 --> 00:04:26.103
Have you ever made pasta?

00:04:26.233 --> 00:04:27.066
- I have!

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.530
Okay, this water, it's fine!

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:30.760
Let's just throw the mac in there.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:31.850
We don't have much time!

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:34.650
- But you need to wait
for the water to boil

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.520
before you cook pasta.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:38.369
Bring water to a rapid boil.

00:04:38.369 --> 00:04:39.900
- Oh a rapid boil.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.050
Okay, alright. I thought
it was like a regular boil.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.767
I didn't -- Rapid!

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:44.678
- How you doing over there?

00:04:44.678 --> 00:04:45.511
- What's up?!

00:04:45.511 --> 00:04:47.177
How's it going?
- Got a little panko, I see.

00:04:47.177 --> 00:04:48.160
- What are you doing?

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.846
Are you stirring your tomato soup?

00:04:49.846 --> 00:04:51.163
- I am.

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.320
Tomato soup.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:54.554
It's got a little red pepper in there.

00:04:54.554 --> 00:04:57.463
Gonna make that into
actually a vinaigrette.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:01.050
So maybe I lied when I said
it won't be too gourmet.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.400
- We're just waiting
for our water to boil.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.540
- Look it! She's already almost done

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:05.790
with the cheese sandwich.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.010
The tomato vinaigrette.

00:05:08.084 --> 00:05:09.450
- Show the sandwich some respect.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.163
It's a grilled cheese.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.674
It's not like just a cold cheese sandwich.

00:05:13.674 --> 00:05:15.537
- Whatever! (laughing)

00:05:15.537 --> 00:05:16.837
- Can we steel some bacon?

00:05:17.006 --> 00:05:18.034
- Yeah of course.

00:05:18.034 --> 00:05:19.830
- When I think cheese sandwich,

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.070
I think like cold and room temperature.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:22.908
Back up, Nnenna.

00:05:22.908 --> 00:05:25.527
Back up, Imma start throwing bacon at you.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.073
- I just kinda mess with her
ingredients a little bit,

00:05:27.073 --> 00:05:29.010
just kick 'em to the side, you know.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.260
'Cause she thought bacon was over here

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.206
move it over there.

00:05:31.206 --> 00:05:32.039
Put that over there.

00:05:32.039 --> 00:05:33.530
There's a whole strategy behind it.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:34.807
- She's gonna go gourmet.

00:05:34.807 --> 00:05:36.640
So we're gonna have to try to up our game.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:37.473
- Right.

00:05:37.473 --> 00:05:38.540
- Make it a little more gourmet.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.530
- What's better than gourmet?

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.980
- The only thing that I
know is gourmet is basil.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.230
- You know, I had a lot of
confidence going into this.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:47.770
- Just because the water isn't boiling.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:49.623
You're losing confidence in us?

00:05:49.647 --> 00:05:52.070
I hope Nnenna is like
actually distracting her

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:53.370
instead of distracting me.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:54.537
- Back up, back up.

00:05:54.537 --> 00:05:55.553
Get out of here.

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:57.270
- So I figured out how
she's making a vinaigrette.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:59.933
She's using a blender to make it happen.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.810
Can we put the macaroni in now?

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:03.973
Please, thank God.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.303
- Okay, okay, okay, okay.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:10.773
- How's that?

00:06:10.773 --> 00:06:11.817
- Are you done with your vinaigrette?

00:06:11.817 --> 00:06:13.843
- The vinaigrette is done, son.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:14.793
- Oh no!

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:16.350
- Don't sound scared.

00:06:16.516 --> 00:06:17.849
- I'm so scared.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:19.960
- Are you guys making a roux base?

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:20.823
- [Inga] Yes!

00:06:20.823 --> 00:06:21.656
- Hmm, okay.

00:06:21.656 --> 00:06:22.489
She knows what she's doing.

00:06:22.489 --> 00:06:23.620
That's a pro move right there.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:25.250
Make sure you cook your roux enough.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.003
Nobody likes undercooked flour.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:28.172
Don't let me scare you.

00:06:28.172 --> 00:06:29.339
- We got this.

00:06:30.751 --> 00:06:32.418
Look at that butter!

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:33.653
You smell that?

00:06:33.653 --> 00:06:34.486
- Hurry up. Gotta go.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:36.213
Listen, Inga.

00:06:36.213 --> 00:06:38.623
If we lose, we're no longer BFFs, alright?

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.633
- Don't let the team fall apart now.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.310
- The team is not falling apart.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.623
I will make this mac and cheese.

00:06:49.159 --> 00:06:50.473
Oh my god, what is she doing?

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:52.070
Nnenna, go check it out.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:54.770
- She's doing the thing that you,

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:56.837
you're dressing up the plate the--

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:58.003
- The thing?

00:06:58.340 --> 00:06:59.173
- [Adrienne] Plating.

00:06:59.173 --> 00:07:00.006
- Plating already?

00:07:00.006 --> 00:07:00.839
- Please, let's go.

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:01.923
- Look, this looks --

00:07:01.923 --> 00:07:03.450
Okay it's coming to life, alright?

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:06.113
Does it or does it not
look like childhood?

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:12.743
What does "Okay" mean?

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:14.800
Do you put the mozzarella cheese on?

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:15.633
- Oh yeah.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:18.000
- [Crew Member] Five minutes.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.200
- Where's the broil function?

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:22.770
I'm just like, twisting the knobs

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:23.610
being like "work, work, work"

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:24.500
and that didn't work.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.333
Help.

00:07:25.333 --> 00:07:27.920
I had to run out and ask
a Tasty producer nearby

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.047
like "Please. Help me win."

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:32.690
Thank you so much!

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:33.663
- Ooh, yeah.

00:07:33.692 --> 00:07:35.843
- Perfect kid size portion.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:38.190
- You know you have a plated,

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.430
kinda chef-fy version of a dish,

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.283
going up against mac and cheese.

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:43.640
Mac and cheese might take it.

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:44.473
You never know.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:45.513
- (both singing) Tada!

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.450
- I think we did pretty great.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:50.200
- I think you guys did really well.

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:52.023
- We're getting our judges up here to

00:07:52.023 --> 00:07:53.990
see what they think of our dishes.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:56.290
- Great 'cause mac and
cheese isn't good cold.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:03.053
- Oh my gosh!

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:04.390
- Oh it's mac and cheese.

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:07.783
- Oh look at their classic,
little mac and cheese.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:12.753
That's some good mac and cheese.

00:08:12.753 --> 00:08:13.660
- It's a little hot.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:14.852
- Whoo! Okay!

00:08:14.852 --> 00:08:15.820
- I like the crunchiness.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:17.040
- It's got a lot of cheese in it.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.470
- The breadcrumbs on top, that was like

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.500
the distinguishing factor
of having box mac and cheese

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:22.610
when your mom was out of town

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:23.870
and then when your mom would come home,

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:25.340
she would make you mac
and cheese in the oven

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:26.390
with the breadcrumbs.

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:27.270
- I'm feeling that.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:28.520
I see what you did there.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.220
- Oh my gosh! Look at this plating.

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:32.053
- Whoa!

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:35.563
- Did they leave any for me? (laughs)

00:08:38.785 --> 00:08:39.618
Mmmm!

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.220
- That is like the fanciest grilled cheese

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.410
I've ever had in my life.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:44.240
- That grilled cheese
has like three layers

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:46.200
of cheese inside of it.
- The tomatoes are really nice

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.030
with the acidity and the freshness.

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:48.863
Can I eat more?

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.100
- So my favorite between the two,

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.900
has to be the mac and cheese.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:53.950
The grilled cheese was so good

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:55.530
and I did have it a lot as a kid,

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:58.480
but I feel like this was
just more close to home

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:01.577
and comfort food and
things you grew up with.

00:09:01.577 --> 00:09:05.663
- Out of these two dishes, my
favorite has to be this one.

00:09:05.846 --> 00:09:09.950
I think this one demonstrates
really well craftsmanship

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:11.520
in terms of taking something as simple

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:13.080
as a grilled cheese and elevating it.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.143
- So out of these two dishes right here.

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:16.103
I'm feeling this grilled cheese

00:09:16.103 --> 00:09:17.270
with the tomatoes on the side.

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:18.680
That's it guys.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.070
I think we have a winner.

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:22.520
- [Crew Member] This
amateur versus pro chef

00:09:22.823 --> 00:09:24.510
childhood favorite foods

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:25.923
- Can we say two?

00:09:25.923 --> 00:09:28.047
It was two versus one.

00:09:28.664 --> 00:09:30.345
- [Crew Member] The winner goes to...

00:09:30.345 --> 00:09:33.428
(imitates drum roll)

00:09:34.065 --> 00:09:36.648
- (all) Ohhhh!

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:40.470
- It's one thing to compete
against fifteen other chefs

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:42.293
and you know their level,

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:43.983
but amateurs, you never know.

00:09:43.983 --> 00:09:45.846
Home cooks are amazing.

00:09:45.846 --> 00:09:48.746
My mom is a home cook and she
taught me everything I know.

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:50.405
You guys could have blown me out.

00:09:50.405 --> 00:09:51.918
Glad you didn't though (laughing)

00:09:51.918 --> 00:09:52.751
- We didn't so.

